 "note": [
  "Scripture is the OLCB 2017 (lug, Biblica, cc-by-sa) — the text language_seed.py names for lg — read from the ebible mirror (lug_bib USX). 'mined' rows were checked mechanically: the cited block contains a run of at least five consecutive OLCB words of that verse; source_file names the Bible edition, not a corpus file.",
  "Rows marked self_rendered include quotations the translator re-personed or re-tensed to fit Clarke's or Susanna's sentence (letters, prayers), and partial phrases too short to verify mechanically; a further ~54 loose allusions and echoes (e.g. 'quiverful', 'olive branches', 'dry bones') are rendered as prose with OLCB vocabulary and not listed.",
  "Book-specific conventions: straight quotes and ASCII apostrophes mirror the straight-quoted English; clock times in Luganda reckoning with the source hour in brackets; 'Mr.' -> Omwami, 'Mrs.' -> Mukyala; Dissenters -> Abakontanya; Methodists -> Abametodisiti; rectory -> ennyumba y'omusumba (matching the shipped susanna-wesley lg bio).",
  "The English (Archive OCR) still carries many scanning slips — stray page marks ('1 *', '15 *'), 'I '11' for I'll, running heads inside paragraphs, and 59 paragraphs of publisher's advertisements at the end of ch16. Translators rendered the intended words and dropped stray marks; the advertisement paragraphs are translated to keep block parity. See the PR for the list.",
  "AI-translated (job #7029); paragraph and tag sequence identical to the English per chapter; awaiting native review."
